## Scope

The directive applies to essential and important entities in sectors including energy, transport, health, digital infrastructure and public administration. Which entities are covered is determined by size and sector.

## Key requirements

- **Risk management measures** under [Article 21](/en/lagstiftning/nis2/kap-4#article-21-cybersecurity-risk-management-measures) – organisations must take appropriate and proportionate technical, operational and organisational measures.
- **Incident reporting** under [Article 23](/en/lagstiftning/nis2/kap-4#article-23-reporting-obligations) – significant incidents are reported to the competent authority within set deadlines.
- **Management responsibility** – management must approve and follow up on the risk management measures.

## Swedish implementation

The directive has been transposed into Swedish law through the Cybersecurity Act (2025:150), which entered into force on 15 January 2025. Supervision is divided among several sectoral authorities with the Swedish Civil Defence and Resilience Agency as coordinating authority.
